Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"deedee|A layover! Where? Never mind. Take a sweater. Take two. Take the crisp.":"","deedee|To the moon and back, Tommy. Both ways.":"","deedee|Tommy! Sit. Eat. I made a crisp. It is nine in the morning and it is a crisp. Do not argue.":"","amy|Go. GO. I have a house to decorate and a cake to hide from your father. Take the girls and get the scoops.":"","boppy|Ice cream? My knee says sit. My knee has been saying sit since 1994.":"","deedee|Not today, honey. The cake is in the oven and the oven doesn't care that it's a birthday.":"","michael|Cold lasagna, one diaper bag, and Isla eating the tablecloth. We're thriving.":"","michael|Hey, Tom. Good to see you. Please ignore the cracker crumbs. They live here now.":"","michael|I heard Olivia say Michael. Whatever it is, I'm on it. Isla, that is not a snack.":"","michael|Yes, Olivia. Heard you. Handled. Lachlan, we do not lick the fence.":"","michael|Zero car keys and one very sticky toddler. Wait. Keys. Gutter. Right.":"","olivia|Michael! Isla is near the curb. Okay. Never mind. Thank you, babe.":"","olivia|My lasagna is a brick. A cold lasagna brick. Michael is guarding it with his life.":"","olivia|Tom! Oh, thank goodness. You already have her. She hasn't slept since Sunday.":"","justin|Amy says I never sit down. I sat down once. It was a playoff game. We lost.":"","justin|Big game tonight. If you hear yelling, that's me. If you hear crying, that's also me.":"","justin|Conference night is over. I survived. I'm going to sit on this couch until Field Day.":"","justin|Deedee’s plate? Oh, everybody waits for Deedee’s plate. She brings one every conference night.":"","justin|Don't tell Gary. Gary eats the whole thing.":"","justin|Every country song is about a truck, a dog or a girl. I got a truck and two girls. Living the song.":"","justin|Fixed the porch light, the garbage disposal and the bunk bed. Before lunch.":"","justin|Grace, Rose, come here. Who's Daddy's favorite? Both. Correct. Go get 'em.":"","justin|Grace, you were amazing out there. Rose, you were also amazing. Also, why are you sticky?":"","justin|Halverson. Fourth grade. I'm hiding in the staff room. That's allowed. It's in the contract.":"","justin|Hey, everybody. The lights all came back on at twelve oh one. So I came back too. I brought bread.":"","justin|Hold this. No, the other end. It's the OTHER banner. Don't touch the copper.":"","justin|If you're hungry, the fridge is a minefield. Every lunch in there has a name on it. Read the labels.":"","justin|It lights up. Every letter. I'm an electrician, Gracie. It was never going to just hang there.":"","justin|Long Island born. Country music raised. Don't ask me how. Nobody knows.":"","justin|Rewiring the hallway. Amy wanted a dimmer. Amy gets a dimmer.":"","justin|The banner's done. Hold this. No, the other end. Don't touch the copper.":"","justin|Those two girls are the best thing I ever built. And I built that deck.":"","justin|Tom. Hey. Hold this. No, the other end. Don't touch the copper.":"","justin|Watch your step, Tom. That board is loose. I know. It's on the list.":"","justin|Take some for the road. Don't tell Gary.":"","justin|It's store-bought.":"","justin|Every conference night. Twelve years. It's the only reason Gary shows up.":"","justin|Heading out? I can come. I have a tool belt, a flashlight and a strong opinion about whatever you're about to fight.":"","justin|Great. Let me grab my jacket. And the ladder. Don't ask about the ladder.":"","justin|No problem. The hallway light won't finish itself. It's been almost done since June.":"","justin|Somebody has to tag out. I'll wait. I'll be on the ladder.":"","amy|Everybody okay? Good. He’s a clipboard with legs.":"","amy|Everybody okay? It calls one of us every turn. Move before it goes again, or Tom will walk you on.":"","amy|Everything, and quickly. I think we’re going to get along.":"","amy|Here’s the plan. Tom up front, girls with me. If that board calls your name, don’t sit there. Move.":"","amy|It’s ringing. It’s just ringing. Mom always picks up. Mom picks up on the FIRST ring. She picks up before it rings.":"","amy|I’m calling her. I’m calling her right now.":"","amy|I’ve heard nothing, which means he’s been saving you for a special occasion.":"","amy|I’ve never been on standby in my life. I’ve been on time, or I’ve been first.":"","amy|My daughters ran out of the house in their socks, Tom. I’m their ride home. And I’m faster than you.":"","amy|Nine gates. Boston, Denver, Seattle, Chicago, Miami. Every one of them says PAUSED.":"","amy|Nobody has claimed the retainer in my family since 2011. That’s not related. Moving on.":"","amy|Nobody is cancelling you. You just never got a boarding pass. Here. Take mine.":"","amy|STOP THE PLANE. I have a ticket. I don’t have a ticket. I have my running shoes.":"","amy|That’s either the nicest thing I’ve ever heard or a threat.":"","amy|That’s what the person who loses says.":"","amy|Then we’re in the layover. Between the two. Everything is on time and nothing is going anywhere.":"","amy|You stopped our clocks. You stopped MY clock.":"","amy|You’re the boyfriend.":"","boppy|Bring me back a pretzel. A real one. Not the airport kind.":"","boppy|Don’t throw it out. It’s warm. I think it’s warm. My knee says it’s warm.":"","boppy|This came for the recliner. A gold card. “Priority Member.” Junk mail. They send it to the recliner now.":"","grace|Hi! I’m Grace. I’m nine.":"","grace|It’s a whole day of everybody’s trip, stopped in the middle. The seagull still has the fry.":"","grace|Paused isn’t happy. Paused is stuck.":"","grace|Rose, he has a paddle that says STANDBY and he thinks it’s a weapon.":"","grace|Rose, when it calls you, move. Don’t stop to look at anything.":"","grace|Tata, if you tell Mom, I’m going to make a video about it. Please like and subscribe.":"","grace|Tata. Every single thing here has a tag. A blue mitten. A trombone. A birthday hat. A retainer.":"","grace|Tata. The little green town. It’s turning orange. No. Amber. Like a caution light.":"","grace|Tata. The window. There are two tiny towns in it.":"","grace|Thank you. Subscribe.":"","grace|That is the saddest thing I have ever read. And I read my sister’s diary.":"","grace|We weren’t hiding. We were pre-boarding. Rose got the good blanket.":"","la_woman|DING. Attention, passengers. The departures board has been updated.":"","la_woman|DING. Flight Zero from Los Angeles has arrived at the Jet Bridge. Welcome to the layover. Please do not feed the dog the pretzels.":"","la_woman|DING. LONG ISLAND: CLOSED. LOS ANGELES: NOW BOARDING.":"","la_woman|DING. Welcome aboard Flight Zero, nonstop to Wherever. Please stow your bags, your seatbacks, and your questions.":"","la_woman|DING. Welcome to Terminal Infinity. It is always dusk. Every flight is on time.":"","la_woman|Ladies and gentlemen, we are experiencing a little weather. It is not the kind with rain. Please look out the window.":"","rose|...I looked at one thing.":"","rose|BOO! We’re stowaways! Tata, what’s a stowaway?":"","rose|Can I ring the bell?":"","rose|Can we live here? There’s a plant with a hat.":"","rose|I don’t have a diary. I have a drawing of a dog.":"","rose|I rang it gently. It rang back less gently.":"","rose|I was going to look at it with my face.":"","rose|I wasn’t going to.":"","rose|I won’t look at anything.":"","rose|Is Deedee okay?":"","rose|It’s ours now.":"","rose|It’s the one with the tiny planes on it.":"","rose|I’m Rose. I’m six. I’m on a longboard.":"","rose|Tata. Tata. The ? suitcases. They’re all in here. They’re all being very polite.":"","rose|The seagull has had that fry for a hundred years. He’s not happy. He’s hungry.":"","rose|The sky has a hole in it. The hole is pink. Tata, can I touch the hole?":"","rose|Which one is Los Angeles?":"","tnb|And you’re the sister. The runner. I’ve heard a lot.":"","tnb|Both, probably. That’s how the good ones are.":"","tnb|Hey, babe. The airline lost my bag, found my dog, and upgraded us both. This place is nice.":"","tnb|Hey. We’ll go get them. Whatever he did, we’ll fix it. Things come apart. I fix things.":"","tnb|I came through the sky with a dog on a pillow. It was fine. There was a pot on the cart that was kind of incredible.":"","tnb|I can fix a handle or fire a vase. What are you good at?":"","tnb|I have a vase in the kiln in Los Angeles. It’s been in there a long time. It’s going to crack.":"","tnb|I know exactly who you are. Tom shows me all your videos. You’re very good at telling people to subscribe.":"","tnb|Okay. Everybody. Sleepover rules. We have a blanket, a dog, and nine hours of dusk.":"","tnb|That’s my longboard.":"","tnb|That’s what happens when you leave something at its best. It doesn’t stay good. It just stays.":"","tnb|These are all things people left behind when they got to the good part of a trip. A mitten from the best snow day. A hat from the best party.":"","tnb|They didn’t want to leave. So they didn’t go back for it.":"","tnb|Tom, build the fort. I’ll make the snacks.":"","tom|...He’s been holding a spot for me. Not for my bag. For me.":"","tom|A pod seat. A real one. Somebody upgraded me and nobody told me why.":"","tom|And it’s where Nara and TNB live. It’s home. Our other home.":"","tom|And something in seat 5B is giggling.":"","tom|Both of them inside glass. Like snow globes.":"","tom|Careful. A town paused is still a town. Don’t lick the glass.":"","tom|Dad’s in his recliner. Mom has the crisp. They’re fine. They’re probably fine.":"","tom|Everybody hold on to something. Preferably each other.":"","tom|Gate Infinity is the big door at the far end. There’s a checkpoint in the middle, and somebody is standing in it.":"","tom|Hi. Hi, bean. Yes. I know. You were so brave on the plane.":"","tom|I wasn’t going to argue.":"","tom|If somebody gets called and can’t move, I’ll walk them on. And if we need a friend in a hurry, wave to the bench.":"","tom|It’s a person who hides on a plane they weren’t invited to.":"","tom|It’s warm. Whatever Vance was holding, it wasn’t his.":"","tom|Left one is green. That’s Long Island. Right one is orange. That’s Los Angeles.":"","tom|My boarding pass is buzzing in my pocket. It says: YOUR LAYOVER IS NOW BOARDING.":"","tom|No touching, please.":"","tom|No, thank you. We have a connection to make.":"","tom|Nobody here is racing.":"","tom|Nobody is subscribing to a stowaway.":"","tom|Sit down. Everybody. Deep breath.":"","tom|Somebody collected them. Every gold clock is the same little clock as the coins.":"","tom|Something is dropping out of the gate clock. A gold coin, with a little clock face. Number nine.":"","tom|Stay behind me. If he sends someone to the back of the line, we’ll get them right back.":"","tom|That’s the nicest offer anyone’s ever made me. And it was in my pocket the whole time. I had a pass.":"","tom|The orange one. It’s the only one still open.":"","tom|We are not living in an airport, Rose.":"","tom|We’ll go get them. We always make our connection.":"","tom|We’re finding the way through it. East, down the Endless Concourse.":"","tom|Which is illegal. And also, apparently, a family tradition.":"","tom|Who is number seventeen?":"","tom|Whoever is under the blanket: it’s breathing very loudly.":"","tom|You came through the sky.":"","tom|You’re the man in the long coat. At the school. At the airport. At Gate Zero.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"amy":{"voice_id":"HLSHrV3D7Gp6sEFcHNev","name":"AoT Amy (Kind)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"heavy Long Island accent","designed":false},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"brainfreeze":{"voice_id":"kYM9iwUI7t87mhAOBs1T","name":"AoT Brain Freeze","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon villain who is a walking chest freezer: a flat, cold, humming monotone with a slight metallic buzz, deadpan and sulky, slow and heavy, with a lonely sadness underneath that cracks through when he is surprised. Animated character voice."},"carmen":{"voice_id":"8ncJvaxiyfELP457mBLS","name":"AoT Doña Carmen","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her sixties with a warm, firm, proud voice and a light Salvadoran Spanish accent. Runs a pupuseria, generous and no-nonsense, laughs easily. Clean studio recording."},"deedee":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"smiling, affectionate, bright and youthful, never stern","designed":false,"voice_id":"9UrcxKDUU0pvcnFhdfTU","name":"AoT Deedee (picked 2026-10-28)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"grace":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"JVVJ6VsnUPJAdfGmEBGP","name":"AoT Grace (Gretchen)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"oolong":{"voice_id":"2PhKaj7sDKqdDEhqQyhl","name":"AoT Oolong","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly woman in her seventies with a warm, gossipy, conspiratorial voice and a light British accent. Leans in to share secrets, little cackle of a laugh, cozy and sly. Clean studio recording."},"page":{"voice_id":"UnNThlnnIcLaHiWDpFdl","name":"AoT Page","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his forties, a librarian with a hushed, dry, whispery American voice. Speaks very quietly and precisely, mildly scandalized by everything, droll. Soft breathy whisper. Clean studio recording."},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."}});
